tiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(\\frac{3}{5})^{2} &= \\frac{3}{5} \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3 \\cdot 3}{5 \\cdot 5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{25}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2= \\dfrac{9}{25}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148793 #edb/ref 1065 8806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148793 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f0e87aeb-338c-5f8d-be18-59b85ed28aac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148793 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482812 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482812 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482812 #edb/ref 1045 "Decimal and Fraction Operations Applied to Commercial Settings" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482812 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186483489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482812 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e837b878-9a6c-52e2-a519-22b1f1e3ba07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482837 #edb/ref 1080 "0.47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482837 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482837 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1010a43c-fb7e-515d-bae0-b8eed8842553" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482863 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{49}{81}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482863 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482863 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1a4c5101-e4ab-510b-a90b-1f80dc5e7721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483084 #edb/ref 1080 "1\\,\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483084 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483084 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a23b3b85-3b3f-5cad-b5eb-d6d6c2bf5943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483116 #edb/ref 1080 "0.48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483116 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483116 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b26ff19c-06ea-5b77-a484-27ad05fc75d3" #edb/ref 175921860